Z||000000||FieroKyle||12-04-2001||01:05 AM||||Alright, probably gonna get yeld at for it but I got my Fiero to about 145 down a hill, 130 mph on flat. I have the 85 GT with the 85 Speedo. When I hit aboit 125 (or about comes to 5 mph on the other side) the speedo spins really fast like your in a time machine, This normal?<P>The car also held pretty good and no headlight doors flipped up. It was sweet actually.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierokylesig_1.gif">      <P>My Fast 'n Black Car<BR>Kyle - 85' GT||||reg||1
Z||000001||LoW_KeY||12-04-2001||11:35 AM||||I've heard about this happening.. and from what I've heard I guess it is?<P>Mine has that little bar at 120.. I would love to find a 150 speedo that looks like the 120 and put it in there  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I've never had the headlights flip up either.. I mostly know because when ever I let my dad drive this he's a nut, but its cool with me  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>AIM: FierFormula88   <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kcbanner.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||12-04-2001||11:42 AM||||It's normal. Once the Speedo gets pass 3/4 of full scale, it becomes a motor.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Master_Sushi||12-04-2001||01:40 PM||||I had the speedo in my 88 coupe just touch the 10mph mark after going past 85. I was really hauling then. I don't know how fast I was going, but engine was at the end of the yellow line. I had stock height wheels/tires, and the car way very light with nothing in it but me. Speedo never went crazy though <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">. Headlights didn't pop up either.||||reg||10
